  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Bitcoin Core nodes ignore the addrMe field in version messages from Tor and I2P peers. Malicious privacy network peers can currently return a routable IP address that the node may subsequently self-advertise alongside its listening port, risking correlation of a node's clearnet and privacy network identities. The PR description notes this fingerprint was identified by researchers and requires outbound connection to the adversary and non-default port usage to exploit.",
